{"name":"Hemp Fabric","hex":"#b5ad88","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hemp","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tall annual herb, Cannabis sativa, native to Asia.","Various products of this plant, including fibres and the drug cannabis."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hemp"},{"term":"fabric","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An edifice or building.","The act of constructing, construction, fabrication."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with fabric."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fabric"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hemp","blocks":[{"text":"The term hemp is the vernacular English language word designating the plant Cannabis sativa, a plant that can be used to make a wide range of products, and be refined into a variety of commercial items, including paper, rope, textiles, clothing, biodegradable plastics, paint, insulation, biofuel, food, medicines, and animal feed. Along with bamboo, hemp is among the fastest growing plants on Earth and was also one of the first plants to be spun into usable fiber 50,000 years ago."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/La_Roche_Jagu_chanvre_1.JPG/330px-La_Roche_Jagu_chanvre_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hemp","wikidata":"Q7150699"},{"title":"Textile","blocks":[{"text":"A textile is any of various fibre-based materials, including fibres, yarns, filaments, threads, and different types of fabric. Originally, textiles were woven; however, weaving is not the only manufacturing method, and many other methods were later developed to form textile structures based on their intended use. Knitting and non-woven are other popular types of fabric manufacturing. In the contemporary world, textiles satisfy the material needs for versatile applications, from simple daily clothing to bulletproof jackets, spacesuits, doctor's gowns and technical applications like geotextiles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Warp_in_Progress.jpg/330px-Warp_in_Progress.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Textile","wikidata":"Q28823"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Hemp_bunch-dried_out_-seeds_close_up_PNr%C2%B00063.jpg/500px-Hemp_bunch-dried_out_-seeds_close_up_PNr%C2%B00063.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Hemp_bunch-dried_out_-seeds_close_up_PNr%C2%B00063.jpg/1280px-Hemp_bunch-dried_out_-seeds_close_up_PNr%C2%B00063.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Hemp_bunch-dried_out_-seeds_close_up_PNr%C2%B00063.jpg/500px-Hemp_bunch-dried_out_-seeds_close_up_PNr%C2%B00063.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hemp seed","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHemp_bunch-dried_out_-seeds_close_up_PNr%C2%B00063.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Hempseed.jpg/500px-Hempseed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Hempseed.jpg/1280px-Hempseed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Hempseed.jpg/500px-Hempseed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A macro image of hemp seeds","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHempseed.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Konopne_seminko_loupane.jpg/250px-Konopne_seminko_loupane.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/